- description: Actions queries whose findings ABOM records and attributes

# What this suite selects **today** is the upstream set unchanged, so that owning the file changed
# nothing on the day it landed. That is where it stands, not a rule about what it may contain:
# ABOM writes its own findings queries, and one belongs here as soon as it earns a place in the
# default. Adding it is a reviewable diff, which is the point of owning the file.
#
# Every result keeps the `@id` of the query that produced it, and an ABOM-authored one is prefixed
# `abom/`. That prefix is what lets a consumer tell ours from upstream's and filter on either — it
# does the work that keeping the two in separate suites would otherwise have to.
#
# Pinned exactly rather than by range: without `version:` the CLI resolves the most recent pack,
# so the set of rules ABOM attributes could change with no commit here.
- import: codeql-suites/actions-all.qls
  from: codeql/actions-queries
  version: 0.6.37

# The nine `experimental/` queries stay in. Precision is a property of the rule, and a consumer
# filtering on rule id can always drop them — whereas a finding never collected cannot be
# recovered.

# The first ABOM-authored query to earn a place here. It answers what an upstream pinning rule
# structurally cannot: whether the lockfile accounts for a reference at all. `actions/unpinned-tag`
# exempts the `actions` and `github` owners and accepts any bare commit, so a reference either one
# covers is never examined, lockfile or not.
- query: ActionsLockAware/UncoveredActionRef.ql

# Its complement. `UncoveredActionRef` compares a workflow against a lockfile, so it is silent on a
# repository that has no lockfile to compare against -- exactly the repositories least covered.
# This one reports that absence once per repository, so onboarding is measured rather than inferred
# from a rule staying quiet.
- query: ActionsLockAware/ActionsLockMissingForWorkflow.ql
